.TH MILLERX 1 "2026-11-28" "millerX 0.9.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
millerx \- a small file browser with Miller columns
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B millerx
.RI [ FOLDER | FILE ]...
.br
.B millerx
.B \-\-version
.br
.B millerx
.B \-\-dbus
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B millerX
shows every folder from
.I /
down to where you are in its own column, and previews the selected file on the
right: pictures, a video's frame, a song's cover, the first page of PDFs, text and
the contents of archives. A folder's pictures show as thumbnails under its details.
.PP
Without arguments it opens your home folder. A
.I FOLDER
opens there; a
.I FILE
opens its folder with the file highlighted. Each argument gets its own window.
.PP
It needs no service running in the background. Optional programs add more
previews when they are installed:
.BR ffmpeg (1)
(video frames, music covers, AVIF and HEIC),
.BR pdftoppm (1)
(PDF pages),
.B blender\-thumbnailer
(pictures saved in Blender files),
.BR meld (1),
.BR kdiff3 (1),
.BR kompare (1)
or
.BR diffuse (1)
(Compare two files; without them millerX shows
.BR diff (1)
output) and
.BR pkexec (1)
(Open as root).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-dbus
Start without a window and wait up to 30 seconds for a "Show in folder" request
over D\-Bus (org.freedesktop.FileManager1), then open only the window asked for.
Meant for a D\-Bus service file, see
.BR FILES .
.SH KEYS
.TP 18
.BR "Left" ", " "Right"
previous / next column
.TP
.BR "Backspace" ", " "Alt+Up"
up one level
.TP
.BR "Alt+Home" ", " "Alt+/"
home folder, the Computer column (disks, USB sticks, network)
.TP
.B Enter
open
.TP
.B F2
rename
.TP
.BR "Delete" ", " "Shift+Delete"
move to the trash, delete permanently
.TP
.B Ctrl+C, Ctrl+X, Ctrl+V
copy, cut, paste (shared with Thunar's clipboard)
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+N
new folder
.TP
.B Ctrl+F
search names in this folder and every folder below it; Escape goes back
.TP
.B Escape
unselect everything in this column
.TP
.B Ctrl+D
bookmark this folder
.TP
.B Ctrl+H
show hidden files
.TP
.B Ctrl+L
location bar
.TP
.B Alt+Enter
properties
.TP
.B Ctrl+N
new window at this folder
.TP
.B Ctrl+,
settings
.TP
.B F5
reload
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q, Ctrl+W
close the window
.PP
Typing letters jumps to the first name starting with them; the same letter again goes
to the next one. Middle\-click a folder to open it in a new window, a file to open it.
The trash is the last line of the bookmarks menu.
.PP
A program, script or launcher asks before it runs; \fBTrusted\fR runs it and, from then on,
without asking while it stays the same file. What belongs to root in folders only root can
change (what your distribution installed) runs without asking, also after updates; Settings
\(-> Programs can switch that off. Inside a git repository the right\-click menu can have
\fBGit\fR (Status, Log, Diff, Add, Commit, Revert): Settings \(-> Tools \(-> Git, off by default;
a second switch there colours new files green and changed ones red.
.PP
Settings \(-> Unleash \(-> \fBClicks and drags\fR: \fBClassic\fR (the default) selects what a
right\-click is on; \fBUnleashed\fR (once a program of its own, millerX Unleashed) only holds it:
its menu acts on it, the columns stay, a drag carries it without selecting it, and a folder held
still under a drag opens. When the installed millerX is replaced by an update, a bar offers
\fBRestart now\fR (Settings \(-> Unleash \(-> Updates can switch it off).
.PP
USB sticks, cards and discs come from udisks2: a click mounts one (an encrypted one asks for its
passphrase), the right\-click menu has Unmount and \fBSafe to remove\fR. A stick plugged in gets a
notice with Mount; Settings \(-> Tools \(-> Automount (off by default) mounts it and opens a window.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/millerx/millerx.conf
settings (also changed from Menu \(-> Settings)
.TP
.I ~/.config/millerx/sorting.conf
folders sorted their own way, one per line
.TP
.I ~/.config/millerx/trusted
programs you trusted: size, SHA\-256 and path, one per line
.TP
.I ~/.config/gtk\-3.0/bookmarks
bookmarks, shared with Thunar and the GTK file dialogs
.TP
.I ~/.config/mimeapps.list
default programs, written by Open with \(-> Set default
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/millerx/languages/
your own languages: NAME.po (or a compiled NAME.mo), made from
.IR /usr/share/millerx/millerx.pot .
Settings \(-> Language \(-> Your own\&... checks a file and copies it here; it is then
listed as NAME
.TP
.I ~/.cache/thumbnails/
thumbnails, shared with Thunar; cleaned up automatically
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/dbus\-1/services/org.freedesktop.FileManager1.service
not made by millerX: create it with
.RS
.nf
[D\-BUS Service]
Name=org.freedesktop.FileManager1
Exec=/usr/bin/millerx \-\-dbus
.fi
.RE
to have millerX started for a browser's "Show in folder" when no file manager
is running.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TERMINAL
the terminal for "Open terminal here", scripts and Git (may include arguments);
otherwise the first of 17 known terminals that is installed. A known one is told to run a
command its own way (xfce4\-terminal \-x, gnome\-terminal \-\-, ...), any other gets \-e.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR thunar (1),
.BR xdg\-mime (1)
.PP
https://github.com/overcatbe/millerx
.SH AUTHOR
overcatbe
